<Layout title="Can an FIR be Quashed by the High Court? | Rajendra Criminal Law Firm" description="General information on quashing of FIRs under Section 528 BNSS.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <p class="text-gold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Blog</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-navy mb-6">Can an FIR be Quashed by the High Court?</h1>
    <div class="prose prose-lg text-ink/90 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
      <p>The Madras High Court may quash an FIR under Section 528 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita in appropriate cases. This article is for general information only.</p>
      <p>Grounds commonly considered include absence of the ingredients of the offence, settlement in compoundable matters, or abuse of process.</p>
      <p>Each case is fact-specific. Consult an advocate for advice.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-navy/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-navy mb-4">Related</h2>
